{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-type-noetherian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:635d23937ffcdd9088854c43c7a115df298f870b71ec00f19152da46121edffe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6dadef9817efc104e08379b25e1553efcf7da18a7ba91a1b90b5c10b2721eb2e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism.\nIf <MATH_0002> is (locally) Noetherian and <MATH_0003> (locally) of finite type\nthen <MATH_0004> is (locally) Noetherian.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0fa2a67fff1b8863ff64e0f403ed0fae57a7ec52d181e45dbb155c8192b81f1e", "unit_id": "tag:01T6:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-Noetherian-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9316dc4dcd1184c0904c4cce2146bb707a2c800e8d6ca6390e2bfb1ea0ae80ad", "source_text": "This follows immediately from the fact that a ring\nof finite type over a Noetherian ring is Noetherian,\nsee Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n(Also: use the fact that the source of a quasi-compact morphism\nwith quasi-compact target is quasi-compact.)\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b308293a11237f3afa7d336ba7cc22884e19ffc33ae0d62fe008f9db032c50f", "unit_id": "tag:01T6:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-type-Noetherian-quasi-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c3309c80cc1fb297a2db0cd5beb3d3eda8cf01608ac86321e430279977de3c6d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c0df7cbeb01850bce28ec98f8deb26849803a63155582a1695c923a65a95407c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be locally of finite type with <MATH_0002> locally Noetherian.\nThen <MATH_0003> is quasi-separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8ffc83f657bc81dba0fa6c93efc8ba287688ff0e4f190dc912b2614da616f136", "unit_id": "tag:01T7:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{properties-lemma-locally-Noetherian-quasi-separated}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-noetherian}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-compose-after-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:72ac09bf3b389b82a2ad290effd336ebf1a8f95af2d2ad688d37b7dfaaeccd26", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8f06d06062cb6a73346e229025c5a3bc995c13d2db6c9b4d532f95e291efbf32", "source_text": "In fact, it is true that <MATH_0001> is quasi-separated, see\nProperties, Lemma <REF_0001>\nand Lemma <REF_0002> above.\nThen apply Schemes, Lemma <REF_0003>\nto conclude that <MATH_0002> is quasi-separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b91f30332d8a36573e4f703fc83f94ed4d22e4dd72ea50a690ce80d69f5d2fbd", "unit_id": "tag:01T7:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-permanence-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2ab0dcbddc4a63cdc2ab91bdea8902808c7ff8439cd4caa03584d2654f2e6718", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fde9e21c8813a91e9c22af31664a6c2f74e635c3913a7679df4ca90cbb1c4936", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes over a base scheme <MATH_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type over <MATH_0004>, then <MATH_0005>\nis locally of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fb6588dd508cce0a802159b70647cf2daa1e1c3475e8e2dbb01265a851342d31", "unit_id": "tag:01T8:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B \\to C$", "MATH_0002": "$A \\to C$", "MATH_0003": "$B \\to C$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-type-characterize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-compose-finite-type}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09700d048300cb70d79fc6b5b8f1631e556837544f6e68169bfd5d6e64eb1946", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:15e71c75029bfcfb160065ac453cd4ba82092cea3fd89ea1dfe0e4f7179377f4", "source_text": "Via Lemma <REF_0001> this translates\ninto the following algebra\nfact: Given ring maps <MATH_0001> such that <MATH_0002> is\nof finite type, then <MATH_0003> is of finite type.\n(See\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf35fdc7b95beb959f6c366df67e991be64b412b43f42c944b2abf8f95c3abc3", "unit_id": "tag:01T8:proof"}
